    "engravings": "Movement: serial 29390814; 21 JEWELS; Colonial Riverside; Waltham, U.S.A.; ADJ. TEMP. Winding wheel also marked JEWELED MAIN WHEEL.",
    "notes": "Three intake images reviewed. Movement architecture, 21-jewel count, bridge layout, Colonial Riverside engraving and serial range are consistent with Waltham's high-grade 12-size Colonial family, most plausibly Grade No. 221 / Model 1924 Col.B. The movement appears visually complete in the supplied rear photograph, but running condition is not established. The dial is in very poor cosmetic condition with extensive spotting, oxidation/finish loss and dark deterioration around much of the numeral ring. All visible hands are missing: hour, minute and subsidiary seconds. The gold-tone central dial area is heavily marked. The bow and crown are present. Case shows age-related wear and darkening but no obvious major deformation in the supplied views.",
    "history": "Waltham's 12-size Model 1924 Colonial B family was part of the company's later slim pocket-watch production. Pocket Watch Database records Grade No. 221 examples as 12-size, 21-jewel, open-face, nickel-finished, pendant-set bridge movements with Breguet hairsprings. The database notes factory-record inconsistencies: some movements in Grade 221 runs are physically marked 'Riverside' and '#1271', so movement engraving and serial-run data do not always align perfectly. A documented Grade 221 run shows total production of 38,125 across nine runs. Comparable serials in the 28.8-29.3 million range are dated to the mid-1930s, supporting a circa 1936-1937 date for this example. The Keystone Victory case grade is documented as 10K rolled gold plate and appears in 1925 and 1932 catalog references, fitting the period of this movement.",
    "warnings": "Do not polish the dial. Its printed/painted finish is already severely compromised and may be extremely fragile. Do not attempt to fit hands until the hand-setting train, hand-hole sizes and cannon pinion/hour wheel are inspected. Avoid aggressive polishing of the rolled-gold case because wear-through cannot be reversed. The 'Beau Monde' dial inscription is not yet explained; do not advertise this as a documented Waltham Beau Monde model without further evidence.",
    "listingText": "Circa 1936-37 American Waltham Colonial Riverside 21-jewel slim open-face pocket watch, movement serial 29390814, in a Keystone Victory 10K rolled-gold-plate case. High-grade 12-size Waltham movement with jeweled main wheel and temperature adjustment. The unusual two-tone Art Deco dial is signed 'Waltham 21 Jewels' and 'Beau Monde'. This example requires restoration: the dial has substantial finish deterioration and the hour, minute and subsidiary-seconds hands are missing. Mechanical condition and timing to be confirmed after service.",
