    "title": "c.1936 Waltham Colonial Riverside 21J 12s Pocket Watch - Keystone Victory 10K RGP",
    "text": "AUD working targets. Current condition is materially below normal market examples because all hands are missing and the dial has severe finish deterioration. A close serial Waltham Colonial Riverside 21J in 10K gold-filled case sold at auction for US$50, while running Colonial Riverside/Riverside 21J 12-size examples have sold around US$225 and current asking prices for Grade 221 examples are commonly around US$180-250, with cleaner premium dealer examples higher. For this watch, treat A$90 as an as-is/quick-floor figure, around A$220 as a realistic target after successful mechanical restoration with sympathetically sourced hands but retaining the distressed original dial, and about A$320 as an optimistic result only if it runs strongly after service, the case presents well and the unusual dial attracts collector interest. A correct replacement/original dial could materially change value, but replacing the dial would sacrifice the unusual 'Beau Monde' provenance unless documented and preserved."
