  "diagnosis": "Known faults are missing hour, minute and subsidiary seconds hands plus severe dial deterioration. The movement itself appears visually complete but has not yet been function-tested. Identification is strongly consistent with Waltham Colonial Riverside, probable Grade No. 221 / Model 1924 Col.B, circa 1936-37. The 'Beau Monde' dial signature remains unresolved and should be treated as a research question rather than a confirmed Waltham model designation.",
  "repairPerformed": "",
  "service": "Full mechanical service recommended if the balance/train prove fundamentally sound; sympathetic cosmetic conservation rather than dial refinishing",
  "serviceNotes": "Preserve the original dial. Source hands only after measuring all three fittings. Verify case serial and Grade 221 identification during uncasing.",
  "researchBrief": {
    "summary": "High-grade later Waltham 12-size Colonial Riverside with 21-jewel movement serial 29390814, probably Grade 221 / Model 1924 Col.B, c.1936-37, cased in Keystone Victory 10K rolled gold plate. It is a worthwhile restoration candidate mechanically, but the dial is severely deteriorated and all hands are missing. The unusual 'Beau Monde' dial inscription could add interest but is not yet documented as a Waltham factory model name.",
    "technicalNotes": "Pocket Watch Database records Grade 221 as 12s, 21j, open-face, nickel, pendant-set, bridge plate and Breguet hairspring, with total production of 38,125 across nine runs. Factory serial records for this family are known to be inconsistent with physical Riverside/#1271 markings, so the visible movement engraving should be retained as primary evidence. Keystone Victory is documented as a 10K rolled-gold-plate case grade. Movement engraving on this example additionally states JEWELED MAIN WHEEL and ADJ. TEMP.",
    "valuationConfidence": "Moderate",
    "valuationBasis": "Condition drives the value sharply downward compared with clean running examples. Recent/visible market evidence ranges from a close-serial Colonial Riverside 21J in 10K gold-filled case sold for US$50 to running 21J Colonial Riverside/Riverside examples around US$225, with current asking prices around US$180-250 and premium dealer examples higher. Missing hands and a badly degraded dial mean the watch should not be valued like a complete example until restored.",
    "partsLeads": [
      {
        "part": "Hour/minute/seconds hands",
        "reference": "Waltham 12-size Colonial family - exact hole sizes must be measured",
        "compatibility": "Do not buy by Grade 221 name alone; measure hand holes and lengths first",
        "confidence": "High that hands are required; low for any unmeasured listing",
        "source": "https://thepartspreserve.com/products/vintage-12s-waltham-colonial-riverside-premier-21j-pocket-watch-movement-no-221",
        "notes": "Aim for period-correct dark/blued or matching Art Deco hands appropriate to the dial; preserve any originals if discovered"
      }
    ],
    "repairPlan": [
      "Verify whether the movement will safely start with minimal power",
      "Uncase and protect the fragile dial before any mechanical cleaning",
      "Measure hour, minute and seconds hand fittings",
      "Inspect motion works and seconds pinion for damage before sourcing hands",
      "Perform full service if balance/train/barrel condition is viable",
      "Fit sympathetic replacement hands and regulate",
      "Retain original dial and document the unresolved 'Beau Monde' signature"
